:"Thanks to Mike Halpenny for this map of all the features of significance on the Red Mo.","caption":"Red Mo River Map","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Mike Halpenny","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/883171","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/883171"}},{"id":"881659","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"884255","description":"Brad Nelson setting the Red Mo race record: 39:29 in 1993.","caption":"Red Mo race","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/881659","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/881659"}},{"id":"890700","ext":"jpg","post_id":"894638","description":null,"caption":null,"poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":null,"poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890700","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890700"}},{"id":"10111","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9608","description":"section below rt 53, paddler in Discovery 174 is Jeremy Davis","caption":"Typical Red Mo","poi_name":"none","subject":"Typical Red Mo","author":"Rand McFarland (KHCC)","poi_id":"102721","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10111","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10111"}},{"id":"881223","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"883731","description":"Pre-race preparations.","caption":"Red Mo Race 2012","poi_name":"Peale Bridge Put-in","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":"102719","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/881223","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/881223"}}],"detail":{"id":"1643","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"The classic Central PA introduction to class II whitewater!  The tainted Moshannon Creek is affectionally known as \"Red Mo\".  If you love the whitewater features of Spring Creek in Bellefonte, PA, Red Mo is the next logical step in the progression.\n\nThe last weekend of every March, Tussey Mountain Outfitters organizes Pennsylvania's longest running downriver race...\n\nRed Moshannon Downriver Race\n\nThis race is held in the Spring on a remote 7.5 mile section of Moshannon Creek.  It starts at Peale Bridge near the town of Grassflat PA, and ends at the Route 53 Bridge near the town of Moshannon PA.  At moderate levels and typical temperatures for this time of year, this section is rated Class II.\n\nThere are classes for solo and tandem open canoes, kayaks, and decked canoes.  Racers can also participate in the \"poker race\" by picking up cards along the race course - the best hand wins.\n\nThe Red Mo Race was begun in 1967. The Penn State Outing Club Canoe Division ran the race from 1967 to 1980. There was no race in 1976. The 1981 race was jointly sponsored by PSOC and Tussey Mountain Outfitters. TMO has run the race since 1982. Boat classes have varied over the years and the [race history](http://www.tusseymountainoutfitters.com/go/dwn_redmo) reflects the awards made in each year.\n\n[Sierra Club column - \"Helping Out on the Red Mo\"](http://pennsylvania.sierraclub.org/moshannon/OTT/OTT06-04RedMoRace.htm)\n\n![](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/archive/medium/883171.jpg?no_cache=1950001)","averageGradient":"28","maxGradient":"0","length":"7.1","correlations":[{"reachID":"1643","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"350","beginMediumRunnable":"550","beginHighRunnable":"1525","endHighRunnable":"2500"},"gaug